#include "Header.leaf"

// Demo of the choice systems, authored with the shared Header.leaf macros.
// Every macro choice disappears after its target node is visited ("Once"):
//   1. $OnceChoice              - once only
//   2. $TimeChoice / $HubChoice - once + time cost; unaffordable choices gray out
//   3. $StatChoice              - once + stat requirement; grays out with a label when unmet
//   4. $FallbackChoice          - writer-authored fallback via !HasChoices()
//   5. Fallback.OutOfOptions    - engine auto-jump when nothing is selectable (time left)
//   6. Fallback.OutOfTime       - engine auto-jump when nothing is selectable (clock at 0)
// Add this file to a ScriptLoader (in place of TestChapter) to run it.

#basePath ChoiceDemo

:: Preload
@function   ChapterPreload

$call SetBackground("bg/Room.png")

:: Start
@trigger    ChapterStart
@cutscene

{@}     Welcome to the choice demo.
        First stop, the plaza. Every choice there is a once-only choice.
        Pick one, and when you circle back, it will be gone.
        When nothing is left, the game jumps to a fallback node on its own.

$goto .Plaza.Hub

// #region DEMO 1: Once filtering + engine OutOfOptions fallback

:: Plaza.Hub

{@}     The plaza. A few folks are out enjoying the morning.

// All three are OnceChoices. Note: inspecting the fountain flows into the
// mayor's scene via $goto - that counts as a visit, so "Flag down the mayor"
// disappears too, even if it was never picked directly.
$OnceChoice(.Plaza.Angler, "Talk to the angler hauling a cooler")
$OnceChoice(.Plaza.Mayor, "Flag down the mayor")
$OnceChoice(.Plaza.Fountain, "Inspect the fountain")
$choose branch

// branches return here; loop until the engine fallback fires
$goto .Plaza.Hub

:: Plaza.Angler

{@Angler1}
        Caught nothing all morning. Used to pull three, four trout out of here easy.

{@You}
        Noted. Something is going on with this lake.

:: Plaza.Mayor

{@Mayor}
        Oh - you're the one from the DNR, aren't you?
        Whatever you find out there, the council will want numbers, not hunches.

{@You}
        Numbers I can do.

:: Plaza.Fountain

{@}     The fountain's basin is spotless. Someone scrubbed it recently.
        While you're leaning over the edge, the mayor walks up behind you.

$goto .Plaza.Mayor

// #endregion

// #region DEMO 2: $StatChoice + writer-authored $FallbackChoice

:: Square.Hub

{@}     The town square. A notice board, a stray cat, and a lookout tower.

// The tower is a StatChoice needing Ranger 2 (your starting value), so it's
// selectable and disappears after the climb like any macro choice. Raise the
// requirement to 3 to see it gray out with a label instead - grayed choices
// stay visible, unlike once-picked ones, which are hidden.
// (To hide a stat-gated choice instead, wrap it in $if StatCheck(Ranger, 3).)
// The FallbackChoice only appears once nothing else is selectable. Because it
// becomes selectable, the engine's Fallback.OutOfOptions never fires here.
$OnceChoice(.Square.Notice, "Read the notice board")
$OnceChoice(.Square.Cat, "Follow the stray cat")
$StatChoice(.Square.Tower, "Climb the lookout tower", Ranger, 2)
$FallbackChoice(.Square.Leave, "Nothing left to do here. Head for the docks.")
$choose branch

$goto .Square.Hub

:: Square.Notice

{@}     "Town council meets Friday. Agenda: the lake."

:: Square.Cat

{@}     The cat leads you halfway down an alley, then loses interest. Typical.

:: Square.Tower

{@}     From up here the whole shoreline is visible. Worth the climb.

:: Square.Leave

{@You}
        Time to see the docks.

// DecreaseTime() spends time outside of a choice - here it burns the clock
// down to 8 so the docks demo reaches zero in two picks.
$call DecreaseTime(12)

$goto .Docks.Hub

// #endregion

// #region DEMO 3: $TimeChoice + engine OutOfTime fallback

:: Docks.Hub

{@}     The docks. Everything here costs time - watch the counter.

// HasTime() lets a writer react to the clock before the engine fallback fires.
$if !HasTime(8)
{@Angler1}
        Light's fading. Better wrap it up soon.
$endif

// You arrive with 8 chunks; each TimeChoice costs 4. Two picks drain the
// clock to 0, and the engine jumps to Fallback.OutOfTime. (If time ran out
// with choices still unpicked, they'd gray out before the redirect.)
$TimeChoice(.Docks.Nets, "Help haul nets", 4)
$TimeChoice(.Docks.Stories, "Swap fishing stories", 4)
$choose branch

$goto .Docks.Hub

:: Docks.Nets

{@}     Heavy work. The nets come up with more lamprey scars than fish.

:: Docks.Stories

{@Angler1}
        ...and THAT one was longer than your arm. Promise.

// #endregion

// #region Fallbacks

// The engine jumps here when a hub has no selectable choices but time remains.
// For this demo it routes onward to the square.
:: Fallback.OutOfOptions

{@}     You've done everything there is to do here.
        (Engine fallback: Fallback.OutOfOptions)

$goto .Square.Hub

// The engine jumps here when choices come up and the clock is at zero.
:: Fallback.OutOfTime

{@}     You're out of time.
        (Engine fallback: Fallback.OutOfTime)
        That's the whole tour - thanks for playing the demo.

$stop

// #endregion
